                [ 'p', 'There is no single per-minute rate for laser engraving. The price is the cost of material, working time and job setup spread over the quantity, plus a markup: price per piece = (material + time × hourly rate + setup ÷ quantity) × (1 + markup). That is why a single piece costs more than the same piece in a batch, and why a laser business needs a minimum order value.' ],
                [ 'p', 'Below we show how to price laser engraving and cutting and how to build a price list and B2B quotes. We don’t give market rates, because they depend on the region, the material and the customer – you get a method for your own numbers. What the laser itself costs and when it pays for itself is covered in a separate article.' ],
                [ 'h2', 'What goes into the price of laser engraving?' ],
